course: dictionary
lesson: 2414
title: Abbreviations: the CV
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An abbreviation is a short way of writing a longer word or phrase. CV is short for curriculum vitae, a Latin phrase meaning "the course of life".
explain: A CV is a page or two that lists your education, jobs and skills. You send it when you apply for a job, so an employer can see what you can do. «A CV is a page or two listing someone's education, jobs and skills; Americans call it a résumé.»
explain: Words around CV give you clues. «Employers often glance at a CV for less than a minute, so grown-ups fuss over every word.» A CV is read quickly, so it must be short, clear and true. Look at the words next to CV and ask: what would fit here?
fact: CV is an abbreviation of curriculum vitae, Latin for "the course of life".
fact: «A CV» is a short, honest document about your skills, results and work.
fact: In the USA a similar paper is called a résumé.
fact: The plural of CV is CVs: one CV, two CVs.
fact: Useful phrases: write a CV, send your CV, update your CV, and a gap on your CV.
exercise: What does CV stand for? | *curriculum vitae | career vacancy | computer virus | county vote
exercise: What is a CV mainly used for? | To order food at a café | To tell the time | *To show your education, jobs and skills when you apply for a job | To record the weather
exercise: Which is the correct plural, meaning more than one CV? | CV's | *CVs | CVies | CVes
test: In the USA, a similar paper to a CV is called what? | a menu | a timetable | a biography | *a résumé
test: «Grown-ups write a CV, send applications, go to interviews.» What comes right after writing a CV? | *Sending applications | Leaving the job | Getting a pay rise | Going on holiday
exam: If you have changed jobs and learned new skills, what should you do to your CV? | *Update it | Hide it under the bed | Throw it away | Shrink it to one word
